    {
      "id": "claim_534ba6931d844a63b8b5663ab3a5b5e8",
      "statement": "The plotting store commits a response to the draft path only when snapped is true; a fallback writes just the snap state (status \"idle\", snapped false, the warning, polyline and distanceMeters cleared) and never the fallback geometry, and savePlot further requires a committed polyline that ends on stops, covers every stop, and carries a pathStopIds list matching the current chain - so fallback geometry cannot be persisted as a direction's base_polyline from this flow (FR-009).",
